{
  "_comment": "Skins that exist only in data.pdb (no .ae4material): a ship record's Customization component = colour preset (slot 0x12fdc2), emissive preset (0x316b81), colour mask (0x7375c5), decal sheet (0x2eb3d0); Gold-tier records add a specular colour (0x674092) and Specular_Multiplier / Gloss_Multiplier floats (0x1d4676 / 0x26691a). Slot 0x4b861d (the Gold pack) is on every ship, the plain ones too: a reference to the gold version, not applied. ae4_resolve.py adds these to resolve.json, ae4_ship_textures.py bakes them as paint schemes (the ship's body material with the overrides), ae4_scheme_variant.py builds a model. preset / emissive_preset = data.pdb names (ae4_pdb_colors.py); emissive_color / specular = values given directly; mask relative to the assets dir; decals = the decal sheet texture. no_iridescence = the skin's material is a _noiri one (no iridescence: dropped from the model). Entries may also be the mod's own (no record or preset: the colours given directly), e.g. nivelian/208's keyart; glass_from = another glass material on the canopy (assets-relative; ae4_ship_textures.py), only such a skin changes the glass; glass_color = that canopy's colour on this hull's canopy shading instead (sampled from the other hull's canopy; no emission), glass_opacity = its opacity x this; clean (0-1) = polished plates: the diffuse's grime, scratches and small painted markings smoothed and the mask's chipped paint closed, the panel seams kept (ae4_ship_textures.cleaned) (ae4_ship_textures.glass_texture).",
